(CHAPTER I) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Importance and Power of Cotton) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Cotton is the fabric of civilization. It has built up peoples, and has) Tj T*
(riven them apart. It has brought to the world vast and permanent wealth.) Tj T*
(It has enlisted the vision of statesmen, the genius of inventors, the) Tj T*
(courage of pioneers, the forcefulness of manufacturers, the initiative of) Tj T*
(merchants and shipbuilders, and the patient toil of many millions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A whole library could be written on the economic aspects of cotton alone.) Tj T*
(It could be told in detail, how and why the domination of the field of) Tj T*
(its manufacture passed from India to Spain, to Holland, and finally to) Tj T*
(England, which now shares it chiefly with the United States. The) Tj T*
(interdependence of nations which it has brought about has been the) Tj T*
(subject of numerous books and articles.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Genius that Served) Tj T*
(The World's Need) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Nor is the history of the inventions which have made possible to-day's) Tj T*
(great production of cotton fabrics less impressive. From the unnamed) Tj T*
(Hindu genius of pre-Alexandrian days, through Arkwright and Eli Whitney,) Tj T*
(down to Jacquard and Northrop, the tale of cotton manufacture is a series) Tj T*
(of romances and tragedies, any one of which would be a story worth) Tj T*
(telling in detail. Yet, here is a work that is by no means finished.) Tj T*
(Great inventors who will apply their genius to the improvement of cotton) Tj T*
(growing and manufacture are still to be born.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The present purpose, however, is to explain, as briefly as may be, the) Tj T*
(growth of the cotton industry of the United States, in its more important) Tj T*
(branches, and to endeavor, on the basis of recognized authority, to) Tj T*
(indicate its position in relation to the cotton industries of the) Tj T*
(remainder of the world.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(America the Chief) Tj T*
(Source of Raw Material) Tj T*
