(For the present, and for the future, as far as that may be seen, the) Tj T*
(United States will have to continue to supply the greater part of the) Tj T*
(world's raw cotton. Staples of unusual length and strength have been) Tj T*
(grown in some foreign regions, and short and inferior fibers have come) Tj T*
(from still others. But the cotton belt of the Southern States, producing) Tj T*
(millions of bales, is the chief source of supply for all the world.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
