(Such figures can be only approximate. The war has brought growth in the) Tj T*
(United States and in Japan, but has certainly reduced the numbers of) Tj T*
(spindles in Germany, Austria, and Russia. It is doubtful, moreover, how) Tj T*
(well the French industry has been able to maintain itself. But the) Tj T*
(tabulation is accurate enough to show the relative standing of the) Tj T*
(various countries. There are, as has been indicated, other standards than) Tj T*
(the number of spindles. The United States, through the fact that it) Tj T*
(specializes, generally speaking, on the coarser fabrics, uses about) Tj T*
(5,000,000 bales of cotton annually, as compared with Great Britain's) Tj T*
(4,000,000. The British product, however, sells for much more. Thus the) Tj T*
(value of the spindle standard is affirmed. England, then, produces well) Tj T*
(in excess of one-third of the cotton cloth of the world; the United) Tj T*
(States considerably more than one-fifth of it, with the other countries) Tj T*
(trailing far behind, but prospering nevertheless.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Individuality) Tj T*
(of the Cotton Fiber) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration: _The cotton fiber--a highly magnified view, showing the) Tj T*
(twist_]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is a curious ruling of fate which makes the spinning of cotton fiber) Tj T*
(possible. There are many other short vegetable fibers, but cotton is the) Tj T*
(only one which can profitably be spun into thread. Hemp and flax, its) Tj T*
(chief vegetable competitors, are both long fibered. The individuality of) Tj T*
(the cotton fiber lies in its shape. Viewed through the microscope, the) Tj T*
(fiber is seen to be, not a hollow cylinder, but rather a flattened) Tj T*
(cylinder, shaped in cross-section something like the figure eight. But) Tj T*
(the chief and valuable characteristic is that the flattened cylinder is) Tj T*
(not straight, but twisted. It is this twist which gives its peculiar and) Tj T*
(overwhelming importance to cotton, for without this apparently fortuitous) Tj T*
(characteristic, the spinning of cotton, if possible at all, would result) Tj T*
(in a much weaker and less durable thread. The twist makes the threads) Tj T*
("kink" together when they are spun, and it is this kink which makes for) Tj T*
(strength and durability.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Though the cotton plant seems to be native to South America, Southern) Tj T*
(Asia, Africa, and the West Indies, its cultivation, was largely confined) Tj T*
(at first to India, and later to India and the British West Indies. At the) Tj T*
(beginning of the eighteenth century, the West Indies, because of their) Tj T*
(especial fitness for growing the longer staples were supplying about) Tj T*
(seventy per cent. of the food of the Lancashire spindles. The United) Tj T*
(States having made unsuccessful attempts to produce cotton in the early) Tj T*
(days of the colonies, first became an important producing country toward) Tj T*
