(side-by-side, passing between three pairs of drawing rollers which will) Tj T*
(be described later. From the drawing rollers the slivers now reduced in) Tj T*
(size, pass between two pairs of calendar rollers from which they emerge,) Tj T*
(not as a sliver, of course, but once more as a lap about a foot wide.) Tj T*
(These laps are usually passed to a ribbon lapper, where six of them are) Tj T*
(placed end-to-end, and unrolled simultaneously, passed between four pairs) Tj T*
(of drawing rollers, and then superimposed, one upon the other, and,) Tj T*
(calendered once more, issued as a lap a little less than a foot wide.) Tj T*
(This process may be repeated as many times as the quality of the yarn) Tj T*
(desired may require, for each drawing process served to straighten the) Tj T*
(fibers and so to render the thread more even and capable of finer) Tj T*
(spinning.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Combing is exactly what its name implies. The lap is actually raked by a) Tj T*
(fine-tooth comb with needle-like teeth of steel ranging from 16 to 90 per) Tj T*
(inch. This involves breaking the lap again and the intricacy of the) Tj T*
(comber rests in the mechanism which it employs for joining the separated) Tj T*
(ends.) Tj T*
