() Tj T*
(For a certain class of goods, where a clean, smooth surface is required,) Tj T*
(it is desirable to singe the goods before the bleaching. This is) Tj T*
(accomplished by passing the cloth, stretched out at full width, very) Tj T*
(rapidly over heated plates, or through gas flames, so that the fine hairs) Tj T*
(or fuzz are singed off, but the fabric itself has not had time to take) Tj T*
(fire. Both sides may be singed and the goods may be passed more than once) Tj T*
(through the flame. When yarns are singed, the threads are passed through) Tj T*
(the flame very rapidly, being unwound from one set of bobbins and wound) Tj T*
(up on another.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration: _Front view of an automatic loom_]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the dyeing operation the cotton piece goods pass through a series of) Tj T*
(machines, the goods being in rope form as already explained, so that a) Tj T*
(number of pieces can be put into each machine, side by side. The wash) Tj T*
(boxes, dye vats, etc. are equipped with overhead rollers, by means of) Tj T*
(which the goods, which have been sewn end to end, so as to make a) Tj T*
(continuous string of them, pass out of the dye, over the roller and down) Tj T*
(into the bath on the other side, continuing to circulate around thus) Tj T*
(until the desired results have been obtained. In addition to the) Tj T*
(preparatory washing and boiling, mordanting and dyeing, there are) Tj T*
(subsequent washings to free the goods from loose coloring matter, and) Tj T*
(other special treatments are frequently accorded them.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Finishing in its special and restricted sense, implies a series of) Tj T*
(treatments, such as stretching, starching, dampening, drying, pressing,) Tj T*
(smoothing, lustreing, glazing, stiffening, softening, and whatnot, which) Tj T*
(are given to them according to the use to which they are to be put.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The printing press is constructed with a large main cylinder \(D\), the) Tj T*
(size being dictated by the number of colors which it must take care of.) Tj T*
(As the printing operation is a continuous one, there must be a continuous) Tj T*
(feeding of the cloth, a continuous inking of the engraved rollers \(C\),) Tj T*
(and a continuous cleaning off of the unengraved surface after the) Tj T*
(inking.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Under each roller, where it is fixed in its place in the press, is a long) Tj T*
(copper trough or pan carrying the coloring material, and in the pan under) Tj T*
(the roller, and extending into the coloring matter, is an intermediate) Tj T*
ET
