stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(roller known as the "furnisher" roller, and, as the press revolves, this) Tj T*
(covers the surface of the copper roller with a heavy film of coloring.) Tj T*
(The surplus coloring is scraped off as the roller revolves, by a long,) Tj T*
(sharp blade or knife, known as "the doctor," and after the roller passes) Tj T*
(this it is quite clean, no coloring remaining on it except that in the) Tj T*
(engraved portion.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Each roller has its color pan with its own color in it. Then, as the) Tj T*
(cloth \(A\) passes between the main cylinder, properly covered by suitable) Tj T*
(intervening materials and the series of rollers, each roller in turn) Tj T*
(prints its own color, and, collectively, the finished pattern is) Tj T*
(produced.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration: _Diagram of cloth printing machine_]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The goods then pass into a drying room and are afterwards introduced into) Tj T*
(a steaming chamber, where they are given a good steaming at a slight) Tj T*
(pressure. This steaming develops the colors and causes them to impregnate) Tj T*
(the fibers more thoroughly. Subsequently, for good work, the goods should) Tj T*
(be washed to get rid of the thickening matters that are mixed with the) Tj T*
(coloring, and then the printing appears in all its beauty.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Printing on) Tj T*
(Full Ground Colors) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The foregoing briefly describes the processes of direct printing. In this) Tj T*
(case, the penetration of the colors to the opposite side of the goods is) Tj T*
(not very good. If a solid and full ground color is needed both on the) Tj T*
(face and back of the goods, it can be had either by the "Resist" or) Tj T*
("Reserve" method, or by the "Extract" or "Discharge" method. In the) Tj T*
("Resist" method, when a white figure is wanted on a black or colored) Tj T*
(ground, the goods are first printed with some substance which will resist) Tj T*
(the action of the dye stuffs. Then, when the goods are dyed, the treated) Tj T*
(part does not take the color and the substance used as a resist is washed) Tj T*
(out, and thus a white figure is obtained on a solid colored ground.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the "Discharge" method, the goods are first dyed in a solid color, and) Tj T*
(are then treated with certain chemicals which destroy the dyed color) Tj T*
(wherever they touch the fabric, these chemicals being subsequently washed) Tj T*
(out where they have been applied, and thus again a white figure can be) Tj T*
(had in the colored ground. By the "Discharge" method, moreover, colored) Tj T*
(figures can also be printed on colored grounds, as certain colorings have) Tj T*
(been developed which are not affected by the discharge materials used,) Tj T*
(hence, a whole series of beautiful colors can be printed on goods) Tj T*
(previously dyed with black or colored grounds, each color being mixed) Tj T*
(with a suitable chemical for discharging the ground color, and thus the) Tj T*
(colors of the printed pattern come out as desired.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Another important process which is applied to both cotton yarn and cotton) Tj T*
(fabrics is that known as mercerization, called after "Mercer" an English) Tj T*
(chemist who introduced the process. Cotton when subjected to the action) Tj T*
