(of strong, caustic alkali contracts violently, but when again stretched) Tj T*
(and straightened it is found to have acquired a distinct silkiness of) Tj T*
(appearance, and under the microscope the twisted ribbon-like fibers of) Tj T*
(the material--already referred to--will be found to have become straight,) Tj T*
(glossy and rodlike, just as a bicycle tire would appear after air was) Tj T*
(blown into it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Cotton may be mercerized either in the yarn, warp, skein, or in the) Tj T*
(piece, the first being more effective. The best and most satisfactory) Tj T*
(results are achieved when the material treated is made of fine long) Tj T*
(staple cotton, either Sea Island or Egyptian, the shorter cottons being) Tj T*
(relatively much less improved by the treatment. The mercerizing does not) Tj T*
(diminish the strength of the material, and gives to it a greater affinity) Tj T*
(for dye stuffs.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Internal Organization) Tj T*
(of Cotton Mills) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The foremen are specialists in their particular departments. The) Tj T*
(warehouseman, at one end, is a judge of cotton stock, and the foreman of) Tj T*
(the weaving room at the other knows how many automatic looms may safely) Tj T*
(be trusted to each weaver on his staff.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In between these two there are, according to the individual mill, a dozen) Tj T*
(or more other foremen, all reporting regularly to the superintendent, all) Tj T*
(captains of their own companies of workers, and all keen, in the) Tj T*
(interests of their own reputations, to operate their departments as) Tj T*
(intelligently, as efficiently, and with as little friction with their) Tj T*
(individual operators as possible. For it is generally recognized) Tj T*
(throughout the cotton industry that profitable business depends as much) Tj T*
(upon the whole-hearted cooperation of the wage-earners, as upon any other) Tj T*
(single factor.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Question of) Tj T*
(Individual Efficiency) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As for the operators themselves, they are so varied, there are so many) Tj T*
(problems which they have to face, and such difficulties which those who) Tj T*
(employ and direct them have to solve, that anything like adequate) Tj T*
(consideration is impossible. From the impersonal viewpoint, leaving out) Tj T*
(of account the human elements, the problems of wages, and the correlated) Tj T*
(problem of trade organization, there remains the question of individual) Tj T*
(efficiency. It is that which we have chiefly to consider.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration: _Inspecting finished cloth_]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The number of men, women, and children employed in the cotton mills of) Tj T*
(the country has increased at a very high rate, but there has been an) Tj T*
(interesting diminution in the proportionate percentage of women and) Tj T*
(children under sixteen years of age employed.) Tj T*
